  "definition": "Radionuclide imaging is a diagnostic scanning method that uses a small amount of radioactive tracer to create pictures of an organ or body area. The tracer is swallowed or injected, then a special camera detects the radiation it gives off so a computer can form an image that may show disease or injury.",
